  "id": "hysteresis",
  "term": "hysteresis",
  "definition": "In this account of shared psychosis, hysteresis means that the path out of a shared delusional state does not simply reverse the path into it. Because of this history-dependent effect, recovery after separation can be fast or slow depending on how deeply the secondary person’s beliefs have been reshaped.",
